// === PREAMBLE ===
// @trope    Red String of Fate
// @category Romance / Destiny
// @source   https://allthetropes.org/wiki/Red_String_of_Fate
// @domain   Narrative
// @scale    arc
// @version  1.3
//
// Laconic (per the wiki): an invisible red thread, from East Asian legend, binds two people destined to
// be together — tied finger to finger, it may stretch or tangle but never break. FRONTIER: an OBJECT
// loaded by myth — the thread MEANS "fated lovers." The discriminator is a [+RedThread] bound on a
// [&Binds] event linking two distinct people: the loaded object makes the pair's union destiny, not
// chance. Distinct from Star-Crossed Lovers (a sundering keeps them apart) — here the thread guarantees
// they find each other.


// === IMPORTS & ASSOCIATIONS ===
import "trl/concepts/index.trl"

assoc red_string_of_fate -> [
  star_crossed_lovers : "the destined-to-meet inverse of",
  the_big_damn_kiss : "the fate that pays off in",
  the_chosen_one : "a romance-keyed kind of destiny like"
]


// === ONTOLOGY ===
// — founded here (the destiny-thread is the discriminator; promotion model) —
prop RedThread  [+Mythological]   // the invisible red string binding destined lovers (East Asian legend)
verb Binds(pair) [+Mythological]  // fate ties two people together by the thread

imply RedStringOfFate -> [Destined, Narrative]


// === ABSTRACT RULE ===
// Naming rule (arc scale): a [+RedThread] BINDS two distinct people — the thread bound on the `thread=`
// role of a [&Binds] event tying $a and $b (with $a != $b), so phase-2 re-checks [+RedThread] on the bound
// thread (STYLE §8). The loaded thread is the discriminator: it makes the pair's eventual union destiny
// (an arc-scale promise paid off whenever they meet), not coincidence — parting it from a chance romance.
rule Red_String_Of_Fate {
  when:
    char $a
    char $b
    $a != $b
    obj  $thread [+RedThread]
    evt  $tie [&Binds(agent=$fate, a=$a, b=$b, thread=$thread)]
  then:
    $tie [+RedStringOfFate]
}


// === CONCRETE VIGNETTE: Your Name — Taki and Mitsuha (anime film, 2016) ===
// Years and miles apart, two strangers keep being pulled toward each other — swapping bodies across time,
// forgetting names but never the feeling, drawn back again and again. The braided cord Mitsuha wears, and
// gives, is the thread made visible: red, looping the two of them through catastrophe and amnesia, never
// quite breaking. When at last they pass on a Tokyo stair and turn — "Haven't we met?" — it is the red
// string drawing taut. Fate tied them; the cord only showed it.

// TAKI — one end of the thread
char taki [+Protagonist]

// MITSUHA — the other, across time and distance
char mitsuha [+Deuteragonist]

// THE BRAIDED CORD — the red thread of fate made visible
obj the_red_cord [+RedThread]

scene the_thread_draws_taut {
  beat 1 {
    // fate loops the two of them through time and forgetting by the red thread
    evt the_binding [&Binds(agent=fate, a=taki, b=mitsuha, thread=the_red_cord)]
    // Red_String_Of_Fate -> the_binding [+RedStringOfFate]
  }
}
